cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or check this proof, please cite it as below."
title: "The value of lambda(4): a machine-derived proof completing Mercer's Section-5 program (Chowla's cosine problem, finite front)"
authors:
  - family-names: "Toledo"
    given-names: "Carlos"
    email: "carlos@carlostoledo.co"
date-released: "2026-09-01"
url: "https://carlostoledo.co/reports/lambda4.html"
repository-code: "https://github.com/carlostoledo1891/cert-machine"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - "Chowla cosine problem"
  - "Erdos problem 510"
  - "Newman polynomials"
  - "trigonometric sums"
  - "certified computation"
  - "exact rational arithmetic"
  - "AI-assisted mathematics"
abstract: >-
  A machine-derived proof that lambda(4) = -L(1,2,3,4): the third exact value of
  Chowla's cosine dip, conjectured by Mercer (INTEGERS 19 (2019) #A4,
  arXiv:1709.06612) alongside a strategy he could not execute. The strategy is
  executed and completed mechanically: the fourteen exceptional families are
  re-derived symbolically (five close themselves), the remaining nine are each
  closed by second-level weight arguments with derived thresholds, and 2,231
  finite cases are decided in exact rational arithmetic. Exactly, lambda(4) is
  the root of 512y^3 - 1227y^2 + 600y + 125 near 1.5195578816428. Includes an
  independent audit walk sharing no code with the proving engine (25,819 sets,
  zero holes, zero refuters) and a referee-grade write-up. Machine-derived with
  Claude (Anthropic) driving certified-arithmetic instruments; not peer-reviewed.
